{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup\/init(_:content:)","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup\/init(_:id:content:)","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup\/init(content:)","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup\/init(id:content:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup\/body-swift.property","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup\/content","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup\/id","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup\/title"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup\/Body-swift.typealias"],"anchor":"Type-Aliases","title":"Type Aliases","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup\/Scene-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations","generated":true}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Scene"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WindowGroup","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Content","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Content","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI4ViewP","text":"View","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/View","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use a ","type":"text"},{"code":"WindowGroup","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as a container for a view hierarchy presented by your","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"app. The hierarchy that you declare as the group’s content serves as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"template for each window that the app creates from that group:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["@main","struct Mail: App {","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            MailViewer() \/\/ Declare a view hierarchy here.","        }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenSwiftUI takes care of certain platform-specific behaviors. For example,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on platforms that support it, like macOS and iPadOS, users can open more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than one window from the group simultaneously. In macOS, users"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can gather open windows together in a tabbed interface. Also in macOS,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"window groups automatically provide commands for standard window"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"management."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every window created from the group maintains independent state. For","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"example, for each new window created from the group the system allocates new","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"storage for any ","type":"text"},{"code":"State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"StateObject","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" variables instantiated by the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"scene’s view hierarchy.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You typically use a window group for the main interface of an app that isn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"document-based. For document-based apps, use a ","type":"text"},{"code":"DocumentGroup","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/windowgroup"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A scene that presents a group of identically structured windows."}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WindowGroup","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI11WindowGroupV","symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"WindowGroup"}],"title":"WindowGroup"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/WindowGroup/Scene-Implementations":{"type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Scene Implementations","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup\/Scene-Implementations","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/windowgroup\/scene-implementations","kind":"article"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/Scene":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Scene"}],"url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/scene","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Scene","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A part of an app’s user interface with a life cycle managed by the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","